{"kind":"artifact","text":"The application cache witness proves the migration this head actually makes, @12 to @13, instead of a migration nobody is performing. Exact clean pushed head 8ad3c0c20b6d374b036f3e4b3dd86ef0ad4f8627 on request/decision-records-ui-recut; local and origin identical by commit SHA and tree hash 1f7e7907, checkout clean. Successor to 222d19f6, republished at the corrected head; nothing at this path changed between f6489c78a and here.\n\nWHAT THIS PATH CHANGES, one file. app_test.go, +49/-65. TestAnOlderProfileCacheIsRebuiltUnderTheNewRules is re-anchored to oldProfile @12, seeds a cached statement with Satisfier removed and its admitted value known, and asserts that replay under @13 restores that exact value and replaces the profile. The comments describe @12 to @13. This is the cache migration witness; codex was right that my earlier internal/workroom artifact claimed it for the wrong package, and the corrected successor b0ccfbed says so.\n\nTHE DEFECT THIS REPLACES. The earlier version moved wantProfile to @13 but left oldProfile at @11 and the seeded observable at the @11 receipt-successor answer. A green run therefore said an @11 cache is rejected and said nothing whatever about @12 to @13 — and @12 is precisely the shape where statements carry no satisfier, which is what the replay must restore. A test that passes without exercising the transition under test reports coverage that does not exist.\n\nTHE CONFLICT RESOLVED HERE, stated so a reviewer need not reconstruct it. This file conflicted with main during the recut: delete-versus-modify inside that one function. This lane deletes the @11 receipt-checkpoint scaffolding, while main had added AllowDeadBasis: true to two acts inside the block being deleted. I took the deletion — those additions die with the block and are referenced nowhere else — then diffed the resulting function against the pre-recut version to check nothing else moved. The only difference is main's own independent change